WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.319 --> 00:00:02.280
We are all trying to preserve

00:00:02.439 --> 00:00:05.560
the rich diversity of European countries

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.239
because if that diversity is suppressed,

00:00:09.759 --> 00:00:12.360
we shall weaken Europe, not strengthen it.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.920
The founders of the European Community

00:00:19.079 --> 00:00:22.439
wanted to draw strength from that diversity.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.319
They fully recognised the scale of the task,

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:28.159
but their aims were much more ambitious

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.800
than just a materialistic vision.

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:35.800
A European war was to be made not just unlikely

00:00:35.959 --> 00:00:37.360
but unthinkable.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.079
We have to strengthen the ability of Europeans

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.720
to act on a European basis

00:00:43.959 --> 00:00:46.959
where the nature of a problem requires

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:48.759
a European response.

00:00:49.159 --> 00:00:52.639
War has not been banished from the European continent;

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.920
I think particularly of the war-torn republics

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.720
of what used to be Yugoslavia.

00:01:01.959 --> 00:01:05.479
The healing process symbolised by Strasbourg

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.519
remains badly needed elsewhere.

00:01:08.839 --> 00:01:11.600
We have witnessed the triumph of democracy

00:01:11.839 --> 00:01:15.560
and the demise of dictatorship in Central Europe.

00:01:16.959 --> 00:01:19.360
With the collapse of the Berlin Wall,

00:01:19.519 --> 00:01:21.600
the Iron Curtain has fallen.

00:01:22.639 --> 00:01:27.400
Our task now is to tend and nurture the green shoots

00:01:27.639 --> 00:01:29.759
of a democratic spring.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.280
The Community is especially well-suited to this task.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.879
New members are knocking at the door.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.280
We should be confident of opening it to them.

00:01:41.439 --> 00:01:45.200
We must ensure that the friendship and mutual respect

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:48.280
which we have built among ourselves

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.879
should extend more widely throughout our continent

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.079
and enrich our relations with the wider world.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.800
It is a worthy ambition true to the conviction

00:02:00.879 --> 00:02:05.000
and example of the founding fathers of the Community.

